# Frontend Design System Implementation Rules

When implementing UI components and styling in the AI Law Wizard application, strictly follow the design system documented in `DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`.

## Color System Rules

### Always Use CSS Variables

- **NEVER** use raw color values like `#1e40af`, `rgb()`, or `hsl()` directly in className or inline styles
- **ALWAYS** use semantic CSS variables: `bg-primary`, `text-foreground`, `bg-card`, `bg-muted`, etc.
- **NEVER** use inline styles for colors: `style={{ backgroundColor: '#f9fafb' }}`
- **ALWAYS** use Tailwind classes: `className="bg-background"`

### Color Usage Guidelines

- Primary actions: Use `bg-primary` and `text-primary-foreground`
- Destructive actions: Use `bg-destructive` and `text-destructive-foreground`
- Backgrounds: Use `bg-background` for page backgrounds, `bg-card` for card backgrounds
- Text: Use `text-foreground` for primary text, `text-muted-foreground` for secondary text
- Borders: Use `border-border` for standard borders, `border-input` for input borders
- Professional blue accents: Use `blue-700`, `blue-600` for headers and trust-building elements (only for specific UI elements, not theme-aware components)

## Typography Rules

### Font Families

- Default body text: Use `font-sans` (Alatsi)
- Legal documents: Use `font-serif` (Abyssinica SIL) if needed
- Code/IDs: Use `font-mono` (IBM Plex Mono)

### Font Sizes

- Use Tailwind's standard sizing: `text-xs`, `text-sm`, `text-base`, `text-lg`, `text-xl`, `text-2xl`, `text-3xl`
- Page titles: `text-3xl` or `text-4xl` with `font-bold`
- Section headings: `text-2xl` with `font-bold`
- Card titles: `text-lg` with `font-bold`
- Body text: `text-base` or `text-sm`

### Font Weights

- Body text: `font-normal` (400)
- Buttons and important labels: `font-semibold` (600)
- Headings: `font-bold` (700)

## Spacing Rules

### Use Standard Spacing Scale

- **NEVER** use arbitrary values: `p-[13px]`, `gap-[7px]`
- **ALWAYS** use Tailwind spacing scale: `p-2`, `p-3`, `p-4`, `p-6`, `p-8`
- Card padding: Standard `p-4` (16px), Compact `p-3` (12px), Spacious `p-6` (24px)
- Section gaps: `gap-3` (12px) or `gap-4` (16px)
- Component margins: `mb-2` (8px) for spacing between elements
- Grid gaps: `gap-4` (16px) for grid layouts

### Responsive Spacing

- Use mobile-first approach: `px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:px-12`
- Scale spacing appropriately: `py-4 sm:py-6`, `gap-3 md:gap-4`

## Border Radius Rules

- Cards and major containers: Use `rounded-xl`
- Buttons and inputs: Use `rounded-lg`
- Badges and circular avatars: Use `rounded-full`
- **NEVER** override with inline styles: `style={{ borderRadius: '8px' }}`
- The base radius is `1.4rem` (22.4px) defined as `--radius` CSS variable

## Shadow Rules

- Cards: Use `shadow-sm` with `hover:shadow-md` on hover
- Modals and dropdowns: Use `shadow-lg`
- Elevated elements: Use `shadow-xl`
- **ALWAYS** include transitions: `transition-shadow` for shadow changes

## Component Pattern Rules

### Buttons

- Primary button: `bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-primary-foreground py-3 rounded-xl font-semibold shadow-sm transition-all duration-200`
- Include disabled states: `disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed`
- Include loading states with spinner (Loader2 icon from lucide-react)
- Standard height: `py-3` (~40px), Compact: `h-9` or `h-10`, Large: `py-4`

### Cards

- Standard card: `p-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-card shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow`
- Glassmorphic card: Use `backdrop-blur-md` with inline styles for background, border, and shadow (only exception for inline styles)
- **ALWAYS** use the `Card` component from shadcn/ui when possible

### Input Fields

- Standard input: `w-full pl-10 pr-3 py-3 bg-background border-2 border-input rounded-xl focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ring focus:border-transparent transition-all duration-200 placeholder:text-muted-foreground text-foreground`
- Icon inputs: Use relative container with absolutely positioned icon (`left-3 top-1/2 transform -translate-y-1/2`)
- Icon size in inputs: `w-5 h-5` with `text-muted-foreground`

### Badges

- Small: `text-xs px-2 py-0.5`
- Default: `text-sm px-2.5 py-1`
- Status colors: Use `bg-green-50 text-green-700 border-green-200` for success, similar pattern for warning, error, info
- **ALWAYS** use the `Badge` component from shadcn/ui

### Icons

- Small: `w-4 h-4` (16px) - Inline with text
- Medium: `w-5 h-5` (20px) - Buttons, inputs
- Large: `w-6 h-6` (24px) - Headings, features
- Extra Large: `w-7 h-7` or `w-8 h-8` (28px/32px) - Hero sections
- Colors: `text-muted-foreground` (default), `text-primary` (primary), `text-white` or `text-primary-foreground` (on colored backgrounds)

## Animation Rules

### Framer Motion

- Page transitions: `initial={{ opacity: 0, y: -20 }} animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }} transition={{ duration: 0.4 }}`
- Hover effects: `whileHover={{ scale: 1.02 }} whileTap={{ scale: 0.98 }}`
- Duration: 200-500ms for most interactions
- Spring animations: `transition={{ type: "spring", stiffness: 500, damping: 30 }}`

### CSS Transitions

- **PREFER** CSS transitions for simple hover effects: `transition-all duration-200`
- Use Framer Motion for complex animations only

## Responsive Design Rules

### Breakpoints

- Mobile-first approach: Design for mobile first, enhance for desktop
- Breakpoints: `sm: 640px`, `md: 768px`, `lg: 1024px`, `xl: 1280px`, `2xl: 1400px`

### Patterns

- Grid layouts: `grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4`
- Hidden/visible: `md:hidden` (mobile-only), `hidden md:block` (desktop-only)
- Touch targets: Minimum 44x44px (`h-11`), buttons: `h-10` (40px) or `h-12` (48px) for mobile

### Container

- Max width: `2xl: 1400px`
- Padding: `2rem` (32px)
- Center: `container mx-auto`

## Dark Mode Rules

- **ALWAYS** use semantic color tokens: `bg-card` not `bg-white`, `text-foreground` not `text-black`
- All components must work in both light and dark mode
- Colors automatically adapt via CSS variables - no special dark mode classes needed

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

### ❌ NEVER Do These

1. Use raw color values: `bg-[#1e40af]`, `style={{ color: '#000' }}`
2. Create custom spacing: `p-[13px]`, `gap-[7px]`
3. Skip responsive design: `w-96` (use `w-full md:w-96`)
4. Override theme variables with inline styles
5. Mix design systems (Material Design, Bootstrap, etc.)
6. Use inline styles for colors or spacing
7. Create custom components when shadcn/ui components exist

### ✅ ALWAYS Do These

1. Use CSS variable colors: `bg-primary`, `text-foreground`
2. Use standard spacing scale: `p-4`, `gap-4`
3. Make everything responsive: `w-full md:w-96`
4. Use existing shadcn/ui components
5. Include hover states and transitions
6. Test in both light and dark modes
7. Use semantic HTML and ARIA labels

## Component Library Reference

### shadcn/ui Components

- **ALWAYS** check if a shadcn/ui component exists before creating custom components
- Use `Button` with variants: default, destructive, outline, secondary, ghost, link
- Use `Card` for containers
- Use `Badge` for status indicators
- Use `Input` for form inputs (with proper styling from patterns above)

## Visual Hierarchy Rules

### Heading Sizes

- H1/Page Title: `text-3xl` or `text-4xl` + `font-bold`
- H2/Section Title: `text-2xl` + `font-bold`
- H3/Subsection: `text-xl` + `font-bold`
- H4/Card Title: `text-lg` + `font-bold`
- Body: `text-base` or `text-sm` + `font-normal`

### Color Hierarchy

1. Primary actions: `bg-primary` (most important)
2. Secondary actions: `bg-secondary` (less important)
3. Text: `text-foreground` > `text-muted-foreground` (importance via contrast)

## Code Quality Checklist

When implementing any UI component, ensure:

- [ ] Uses CSS variable colors (not raw values)
- [ ] Follows spacing scale (p-4, gap-4, etc.)
- [ ] Uses consistent border radius (rounded-xl for cards)
- [ ] Includes hover states and transitions
- [ ] Is responsive (mobile-first)
- [ ] Works in both light and dark mode
- [ ] Uses semantic HTML
- [ ] Includes proper ARIA labels if interactive
- [ ] Follows animation guidelines (if animated)
- [ ] Uses existing shadcn/ui components when possible

## Glassmorphic Design Pattern

For premium UI elements (hero cards, feature cards, role selection):

```tsx
className="backdrop-blur-md rounded-xl p-4"
style={{
  backgroundColor: 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9)',
  border: '1px solid rgba(226, 232, 240, 0.5)',
  boxShadow: '0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05)',
}}
```

This is the ONLY acceptable use of inline styles for colors.

## Design Principles

1. **Professional & Trustworthy**: Use professional blue accents, clean layouts, consistent typography
2. **Accessibility First**: WCAG AA contrast, keyboard navigation, screen reader support
3. **Mobile-First**: Design for mobile, enhance for desktop, touch-friendly targets (44px minimum)
4. **Consistency**: Use design system tokens, consistent spacing, unified patterns
5. **Performance**: Optimize animations, use CSS transitions when possible, lazy load heavy components
